' ============================================================
' RELATIONSHIPS
' ============================================================

' --- fleet dispatch wiring (log-streamer env stamping) ---
VastStrategy   --> EnvBuilder   : build(...)
ModalStrategy  --> EnvBuilder   : build(...)
CommStrategy   --> EnvBuilder   : build(...)
EnvBuilder     --> JobsLogger   : sign_upload_url(job_id)
VastStrategy   --> VastClient   : dispatch_job(...,\nlog_streamer_env)
ModalStrategy  --> ModalClient  : dispatch_job(...,\nlog_streamer_env)
CommStrategy   --> CommEndpoint : response payload
CommEndpoint   ..> AgentPy      : job dict\n(log_streamer_env)

' --- worker startup wiring ---
VastDocker    --> VastEntry     : ENTRYPOINT
CommDocker    --> CommEntry     : ENTRYPOINT
VastEntry     ..> LogStreamer   : spawns bg process
CommEntry     ..> LogStreamer   : spawns bg process
ModalHandler  ..> LogStreamer   : spawns bg process
VastEntry     --> VastHandler   : runs foreground
CommEntry     --> CommRender    : runs foreground

' --- HTTP boundary ---
LogStreamer ..> LogRouter : POST log-append\n<color:#1B7A3E>fire-and-forget</color>

' --- backend internals: service composes three collaborators ---
LogRouter   --> JobsLogger
JobsLogger  --> RedisMirror  : append_chunk\nwrite_meta\ntouch_meta\nread_chunks\nread_meta\nscan_log_keys\ndelete
JobsLogger  --> R2Repo       : write_log
JobsLogger  --> JobRepo      : get_status\nstamp_worker_log_url
JobRepo     --> JobsTable    : SQL

' --- archival wiring ---
BMMain      *-- LogTrigger
LogTrigger  ..> LogRouter    : POST write-logs-to-r2\n<color:#1B7A3E>X-Orphan-Secret</color>
LogRouter   --> JobsLogger   : write_logs_to_r2()
R2Log       ..> R2Logs     : writes objects

' ============================================================
' NOTES
' ============================================================

note as IsolationNote #E1F5FE
  <b>Byte-identical render guarantee</b>
  LogStreamer is a separate OS process, spawned
  by the entrypoint BEFORE Blender.  It reads a
  log file that render.sh / handler.py already
  write via ``tee`` / subprocess.PIPE.  Blender's
  command line, env vars, memory, GPU work and
  output files are UNCHANGED.
end note

note as FireForgetNote #FFF3E0
  <b>Fire-and-forget contract</b>
  Worker advances last_offset UNCONDITIONALLY after
  every POST (success or failure).
  * no retry, no local buffer, no worker-side state
    that could grow unbounded
  * no duplicate lines possible
  * trade: an HTTP failure = 10 s window of logs
    lost forever.  Accepted for alpha telemetry.
end note

note as IdentityNote #FFFDE7
  <b>Per-attempt identity</b>
  Each retry creates a fresh job_id via
  ``create_failover_job(new_job_id=...)``.
  Therefore ``job_id`` alone globally identifies
  one worker attempt end-to-end.
  R2 filename encodes (attempt, job_id); path
  encodes (group_id, chunk_index) so R2 listings
  show the retry story visually.
end note

note as CommunityNote #F3E5F5
  <b>Community fleet parity</b>
  Same LogStreamer, same wire protocol, same R2
  layout.  Sidecar lives INSIDE the docker
  container (Dockerfile.cycles COPY + ENTRYPOINT
  change).  agent.py on the host is untouched --
  the render happens in the container regardless.
  Step-0 audit (pre-Phase-1) verifies telemetry
  field parity between community/vast/modal.
end note

note as ScheduleNote #E8F5E9
  <b>Schedule reuse + strict layering</b>
  backup_monitor is a DUMB scheduler.  LogWriteTrigger
  is one HTTP POST per tick.  It has no Redis client,
  no R2 client, no DB connection for this concern.
  All log-storage knowledge lives in the jobs_logger
  submodule, split three ways per SRP:
    * JobsLoggerRedisMirror -- Redis I/O
    * JobsLoggerR2Repository    -- R2 I/O + path builder
    * JobRepository (+1 method) -- Postgres stamp
  JobsLoggerService is pure orchestration and holds
  no store I/O.  Schema changes never require a
  backup_monitor redeploy.
  Redis TTL 10 min + 60 s cadence -> 10 write
  attempts before auto-expiry.
end note

note as NamingRule #FCE4EC
  <b>Naming rule (from feedback memory)</b>
  Every param / field / dict-key here is named
  after WHAT IT IS: ``log_streamer_env`` (not
  ``extra_env``), ``jobs_logger_hmac_secret``
  (not ``secret``), ``LogStreamerEnvBuilder``
  (not ``EnvHelper``).  Reject generic names on
  sight -- the name IS the API.
end note

